{"title":"2024 AIME II Problems/Problem 1","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\" /><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Problem\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution_&amp;_More_by_MegaMath\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution &amp; More by MegaMath</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#Solution_1\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 1</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-4\"><a href=\"#Solution_2\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">4</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 2</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-5\"><a href=\"#Solution_3\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">5</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 3</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-6\"><a href=\"#Solution_4\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">6</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 4</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-7\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">7</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-8\"><a href=\"#See_also\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">8</span> <span class=\"toctext\">See also</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2024_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_1&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Among the 900 residents of Aimeville, there are 195 who own a diamond ring, 367 who own a set of golf clubs, and 562 who own a garden spade. In addition, each of the 900 residents owns a bag of candy hearts. There are 437 residents who own exactly two of these things, and 234 residents who own exactly three of these things. Find the number of residents of Aimeville who own all four of these things.\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Video_Solution_.26_More_by_MegaMath\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution_&amp;_More_by_MegaMath\">Video Solution &amp; More by MegaMath</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2024_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_1&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution &amp; More by MegaMath\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=3ZuOIsVZhdA\">https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=3ZuOIsVZhdA</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_1\">Solution 1</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2024_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_1&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 1\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/8/5/485d49a1ce6105b267fa45aedcbc484ea035919c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$w,x,y,z$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"66\" height=\"11\" /> denote the number of residents who own <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/3/c/f3c13f88915d101b401e1fdeac1b195262655caa.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1,2,3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"43\" height=\"16\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/c/c7cab1a05e1e0c1d51a6a219d96577a16b7abf9d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$4$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> of these items, respectively. We know <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/f/2/af288705c0bb2977050017932f81270a1c390750.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$w+x+y+z=900$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"163\" height=\"17\" />, since there are <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/d/d/fdd4beaeec1aa15c400a0763d78937b0385924b1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$900$\" width=\"26\" height=\"12\" /> residents in total. This simplifies to\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/a/7/3a741b248e7ed1a3dbdd2339706dbe01ee8cd363.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$w+z=229$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"98\" height=\"15\" />, since we know <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/2/a/12a8849c993206b198ce2cda06e24334d8305a79.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x=437$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"64\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/1/9/019fa884bfff0b94ef4a0084d7acd681579b3699.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y=234$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"63\" height=\"17\" />.\n</p><p>Now, we set an equation of the total number of items. We know there are <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/f/c/4fc91a74e299a11765b50170bfa253f2de6d36f6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$195$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"26\" height=\"13\" /> rings, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/d/a/8da56bdf45f3e0e70df55d864dc8c60d2852f94c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$367$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"29\" height=\"14\" /> clubs, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/b/f/cbf97ae5f15fe2016a22eb67c69ef5ad26227fa0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$562$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"29\" height=\"14\" /> spades, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/d/d/fdd4beaeec1aa15c400a0763d78937b0385924b1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$900$\" width=\"26\" height=\"12\" /> candy hearts. Adding these up, there are <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/5/7/e5711c8d31d3bc3119aba377c9bda0f9dfb14e4b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2024$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"36\" height=\"13\" /> (wow! the year!) items in total. Thus, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/7/0/370d8ef5649623d097a2b88d44ed65c39e2cb2e8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$w+2x+3y+4z=2024$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"199\" height=\"17\" /> since we are not adding the number of items each group of people contributes, and this must be equal to the total number of items.\n</p><p>Plugging in <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/9/2/092e364e1d9d19ad5fffb0b46ef4cc7f2da02c1c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"11\" height=\"13\" /> once more, we get <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/e/e/4ee067a747db271bdf64cfe84ecb5f9d30fc0fe2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$w+4z=448$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"107\" height=\"15\" />. Solving <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/a/7/3a741b248e7ed1a3dbdd2339706dbe01ee8cd363.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$w+z=229$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"98\" height=\"15\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/e/e/4ee067a747db271bdf64cfe84ecb5f9d30fc0fe2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$w+4z=448$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"107\" height=\"15\" />, we get <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/5/e/25eb5b30e16b9f5f10d252d1aabc0b8b709f99b4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$z=\\boxed{073}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -6px\" width=\"74\" height=\"25\" />\n</p><p>-Westwoodmonster\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_2\">Solution 2</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2024_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_1&amp;action=edit&amp;section=4\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 2\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>We know that there are <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/f/c/4fc91a74e299a11765b50170bfa253f2de6d36f6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$195$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"26\" height=\"13\" /> diamond rings, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/d/a/8da56bdf45f3e0e70df55d864dc8c60d2852f94c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$367$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"29\" height=\"14\" /> golf clubs, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/b/f/cbf97ae5f15fe2016a22eb67c69ef5ad26227fa0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$562$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"29\" height=\"14\" /> garden spades, so we can calculate that there are <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/5/9/65951211394f21ea1361ac3c84c91bf605c7c481.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$195+367+562=1124$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"189\" height=\"15\" /> items, with the exclusion of candy hearts which is irrelevant to the question. There are <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/b/9/cb93ff37e0c55c9a644b01582858b8f552a50d2c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$437$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"27\" height=\"13\" /> people who owns <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/c/41c544263a265ff15498ee45f7392c5f86c6d151.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> items, which means <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/e/dce34f4dfb2406144304ad0d6106c5382ddd1446.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> item since candy hearts are irrelevant, and there are <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/1/5/815c3c71386b6a6a5d2b338754331461641cc8d7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$234$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"27\" height=\"13\" /> people who own <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/c/41c544263a265ff15498ee45f7392c5f86c6d151.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> items plus a bag of candy hearts, which means that the 234 people collectively own <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/1/1/b1195b7481e6c1134fb13d4fef6eab2dc3a14eef.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$234*2=468$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"107\" height=\"14\" /> items. We can see that there are <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/9/1/c91ecdf399a48f9a8437083760846c4bca88fbb9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1124-437-468=219$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"189\" height=\"15\" /> items left, and since the question is asking us for the people who own <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/c/c7cab1a05e1e0c1d51a6a219d96577a16b7abf9d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$4$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> items, which means <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/c/d/7cde695f2e4542fd01f860a89189f47a27143b66.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> items due to the irrelevance of candy hearts, we simply divide <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/3/6/4361d7d981ed0ed478b57ae16abc615187082075.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$219$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"26\" height=\"13\" /> by <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/c/d/7cde695f2e4542fd01f860a89189f47a27143b66.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> and get <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/a/3/4a371d04038cf86a055eb74d5cde941565ff184c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$219/3=\\boxed{073}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -6px\" width=\"110\" height=\"25\" />.\n</p><p>~Callisto531\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_3\">Solution 3</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2024_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_1&amp;action=edit&amp;section=5\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 3\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/d/c7d457e388298246adb06c587bccd419ea67f7e8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" /> be the number of people who have exactly one of these things and let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/1/3/8136a7ef6a03334a7246df9097e5bcc31ba33fd2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"10\" height=\"14\" /> be the number of people who have exactlty four of these objects. We have <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/e/c/2ec34286e2ba6844731e6a098decdeb6b1992da0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a + 437 + 234 + d = 900,$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"199\" height=\"18\" /> so <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/7/4/7744217f8b2a203ef9696d5479515478873e9f0a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a + d = 229.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"100\" height=\"16\" />\n</p><p><br />\nIncluding those who have more than one object, we have\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/4/9/2496e6635d55828094e22a49b32d7bc9d89ad3ed.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[195 + 367 + 562 + 900 = a + 2\\cdot 437 + 3\\cdot 234 + 4d.\\]\" width=\"396\" height=\"14\" />\nThis is because we count those who own exactly <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/c/41c544263a265ff15498ee45f7392c5f86c6d151.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> objects twice, those who own <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/c/d/7cde695f2e4542fd01f860a89189f47a27143b66.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> thrice, and those who own <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/c/c7cab1a05e1e0c1d51a6a219d96577a16b7abf9d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$4$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> four times. Solving gives <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/1/6/9168767c89129377830d595b8a86e45a9a93826e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a + 4d = 448.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"109\" height=\"16\" />\n</p><p><br />\nSolving the system <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/3/8/838e2deab5f23263e6a3396d3ccde5761e2bc202.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a + 4d = 448, a + d = 229$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"205\" height=\"18\" /> gives <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/f/2/ef2b79d2018bf54c520ad4a579069932f61c1978.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3d = 219,$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"77\" height=\"18\" /> so <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/b/a/0ba7e2585294c0ce0c759928d4e7ec0023525e5d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$d = \\boxed{\\textbf{(073)}}.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -11px\" width=\"95\" height=\"30\" />\n</p><p><br />\n-Benedict T (countmath1)\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_4\">Solution 4</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2024_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_1&amp;action=edit&amp;section=6\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 4\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/2/4/6241eb6c9ab710ffbf34f96f0f922d4ba65bc4ef.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A_1,A_2,\\ldots, A_n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"115\" height=\"18\" /> be sets. Define\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/4/4/444cce3706ad180d94fc8a60b46e9ccc67bc6f54.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[S_k=\\sum_{1\\le a_1&lt; a_2&lt; \\ldots &lt; a_k\\le n}\\bigcup_{1\\le i\\le k}\\lvert A_{a_i}\\rvert\\]\" width=\"241\" height=\"40\" />\nRecall the formula for the number of elements that are in exactly <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/5/0/f5047d1e0cbb50ec208923a22cd517c55100fa7b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"18\" height=\"10\" /> of those sets.\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/e/a/ceaa4a56459c3992644690ad3e32c8c5a1f019fc.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[f(m)=\\sum_{m=k}^{n}(-1)^{m-k}\\binom{m}{k}S_m\\]\" width=\"228\" height=\"53\" />\nFor <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/9/c/39cf3e35a4981583288d2a7c4b34989916fb7360.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n=4$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"44\" height=\"12\" />, let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/c/c/1cce32eefc0a4d5510ef6237bb5bd001e097fe3e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A=S_1,B=S_2,C=S_3,D=S_4$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"256\" height=\"18\" />. We see that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/f/1/cf1b50860a709ff48ba91b95721924ac25ffbb30.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A=195+367+562+900=2024$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"276\" height=\"16\" />. By the Inclusion-Exclusion Principle, and plugging-in <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/4/6/74613dce6029fcbcfadd61bb936f1ca1c1393723.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m=2,3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"68\" height=\"17\" /> for the above formula, we obtain the following equations:\n\\begin{align*}\nA-B+C-D&amp;=900\\\\\nB-3C+6D&amp;=437\\\\\nC-4D&amp;=234\n\\end{align*}\nSolving yields <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/a/5/aa5dbbe1751281a2880995b016fc9130fe7a4c16.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$D=\\boxed{073}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -6px\" width=\"80\" height=\"25\" />.\n</p><p>~Pieandpi3141592653589732\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution\">Video Solution</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2024_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_1&amp;action=edit&amp;section=7\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://youtu.be/n60sIVSYWlc\">https://youtu.be/n60sIVSYWlc</a>\n</p><p>~Steven Chen (Professor Chen Education Palace, www.professorchenedu.com)\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_also\">See also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2024_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_1&amp;action=edit&amp;section=8\" title=\"Edit section: See also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:80%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2024_AIME_II\" title=\"2024 AIME II\">2024 AIME II</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2024_AIME_II_Problems\" title=\"2024 AIME II Problems\">Problems</a></b> • <b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2024_AIME_II_Answer_Key\" title=\"2024 AIME II Answer Key\">Answer Key</a></b> • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"http://www.artofproblemsolving.com/Forum/resources.php?c=182&amp;cid=45&amp;year=2024\">Resources</a>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b>First Problem</b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2024_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_2\" title=\"2024 AIME II Problems/Problem 2\">Problem 2</a></b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"3\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><a class=\"mw-selflink selflink\">1</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2024_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_2\" title=\"2024 AIME II Problems/Problem 2\">2</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2024_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_3\" title=\"2024 AIME II Problems/Problem 3\">3</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2024_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_4\" title=\"2024 AIME II Problems/Problem 4\">4</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2024_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_5\" 